Prayer timeout is longest for chaotic, shortest for lawful. Timeout gets 
lessend more for chaotic than for lawful/neutral when sacrificing though.

> 2 uncursed scroll $200
> 1 uncursed scroll $300
> 2 uncursed scroll presumably Identify
> 3 uncursed scroll $80
> 2 uncursed scroll $100
> 1 uncursed scroll $80

For these, I can only recommend http://nethack.roy.org/clippy/
I know it's _very_ spoily and some may be opposed to using it, but 
heck... it makes iding stuff a whole lot easier.

> 1 uncursed dagger that does not stack with other 32 daggers I have

If the other 32 daggers are also identified as uncursed, then probobaly 
the one has a different enchantment. Try if it's more expensive in a 
shop than one of the 32. If yes, then it's got better enchantment. 
There's also some lookup table for how much more expansive one 
enchantment makes it somewhere if you're really desperate to find out 
the exact difference.

> 1 uncursed silver saber

See the price in the shop to determine if it's Grayswandir.

> buncha potions (already dipped into unicorn horns)

Tricky... try clippy again, as with scrolls. If desperate, lock yourself 
in, and quaff.

> buncha rings

Damn hard, price ID works badly on them. I tend to burn my id scrolls 
almost only on rings.

> buncha wands

Engrave with them and see the effects. There are only some 4 wands that 
don't give a message that allows you to identify the wand (sometimes, 
engraving even identifies the wand instantly).

> 1 uncursed gray stone $60 (Luckstone?)
> another uncursed gray stone from the bottom of the mine that's not the one
 > general store showed no interest in

The first one will be the luckstone if it's from mines end too.

